  "recommendation": "the CAD's two gates 60 mm apart (x0 + 22 and x0 + 82: 8 mm past the socket, 18 mm before the muzzle, clear of the orange tip's boss): a 1875 us window at 105 fps, so a 30 us edge jitter is 1.7 fps and a 1 % timing part 1.1 fps: the latch trips within 2.7 fps of 105 (the Hasbro ball leaves at 95-100, the worst accepted corner at 104); slit the \u00d83.2 cross holes to a 1 mm beam (crossed in 31 us at 32 m/s) so both gates see the same sharp edge. A bypassed converter (the ESCs on the 20.5 V pack) throws ~175 fps and crosses in 1.1 ms, unmistakable, but it has already left: the pre-feed eRPM check (refuse to feed above the bench's n_105) is what stops the first fault ball"
 },
